# codesystem-url-conflict — D2 regression fixture.
library "CS Conflict".

// A hand-authored terminology whose body binds ONE codesystem decl name (the
// historical "<emitName> System") to TWO DIFFERENT urls via two `system is`
// lines. emitCQL.ts surfaces this as `emit-codesystem-url-conflict`
// (success:false) — a CQL hard error that is NOT one of the 3 structural-split
// kinds the pre-D2 allowlist folded, so the FHIR public path (emit_crl_fhir /
// MCP) used to report a misleading success. D2 inverts the fold to a denylist so
// every CQL hard error EXCEPT the #79 sentinel + the lowerLocalCodes kinds (which
// the FHIR lane already surfaces) is folded into the FHIR result and sinks
// `success`.

terminology "Dual System":
- system is `http://example.org/cs/alpha`.
- code is `x`.
- system is `http://example.org/cs/beta`.
- code is `y`.

concept "Has X":
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Dual System".
